- Pot & soil: 6–8" pot with good drainage; use a light, well‑draining potting mix (mix in perlite).
- Temperature/humidity: Prefers 65–80°F (18–27°C); average indoor humidity is fine—avoid cold drafts.
- Feeding: Balanced liquid fertilizer diluted to half strength every 4–6 weeks (or a weak weekly feed).
- Pruning/harvest: Pinch/harvest tops regularly to encourage bushy growth; remove flower buds to keep leaves flavorful.
- Problems to watch for: Aphids, whiteflies, and fungal issues from overwatering; ensure good airflow.

